#= Terminology & Notes
Flushing = purgining leftover particles so they contaminate the next scan.
    (Voltage holds at endVoltage and the system clears out the remaining particles in the tubing)

Hold = time for the system to stabilize before measurements begin
    (Voltage holds at startVoltage, allows system to stabilize before scan begins)

Scan = active measurment phase where different particles sizes are selected at the different voltages
    (Voltage increases from startVoltage value to endVoltage value)

GUI stores values as strings, need to convert them to floats to use in calculations
=#

#= unpacks all scan timing and voltage parameters from GUI, defines the logic for the SMPS scan states (HOLD, SCAN, FLUSH, DONE), 
defines how the SMPS voltage changes over time during the scan, and sets up termination and reset conditions for the scan. 
Returns multiple Reactive signals that are used in the main DAQ loop to control the SMPS and process data in real-time=#
function smps_signals() 
    holdTime, scanTime, flushTime, scanLength, startVoltage, endVoltage, c =
        scan_parameters()

    # Set SMPS states
    function state(currentTime) #determines scan phase based on elapsed time
        holdTime, scanTime, flushTime, scanLength, startVoltage, endVoltage, c =
            scan_parameters() #reviews GUI parameters to determine current scan settings
        state = :SMPS
        scanState = "DONE"
        (currentTime <= scanLength) && (scanState = "FLUSH") #flushing 
        (currentTime < scanTime + holdTime) && (scanState = "SCAN") #scanning
        (currentTime <= holdTime) && (scanState = "HOLD") #holding 
        scanState = (state == :SMPS) ? scanState : "CLASSIFIER" #checks to see if state is in SMPS mode

        return scanState #rturns "HOLD", "SCAN", "FLUSH", "DONE", or "CLASSIFIER" 
    end

    # Set SMPS voltage
    function smps_voltage(t) #calculates appropriate voltage based on can state returned above 
        holdTime, scanTime, flushTime, scanLength, startVoltage, endVoltage, c =
            scan_parameters() #recalls GUIs parameters 
        classifierV = @>> get_gtk_property(gui["ClassifierV"], :text, String) parse(Float64) #reads and converse classifier voltage from GUI to float
        (smps_scan_state.value == "HOLD") && (myV = startVoltage) #HOLD: stays at start voltage
        (smps_scan_state.value == "SCAN") &&
            (myV = exp(log(startVoltage) + c * (t - holdTime))) #SCAN: increases voltage
        (smps_scan_state.value == "FLUSH") && (myV = endVoltage) #FLUSH: stays at end voltage 
        (smps_scan_state.value == "DONE") && (myV = endVoltage)  #DONE: stays at end voltage, but triggers termination and reset conditions in main loop to start new scan
        (smps_scan_state.value == "CLASSIFIER") && (myV = classifierV) #uses classifier voltage 

        return [classifierV, myV] # Returns array of both classifier and SMPS voltages

